{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_49","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\nIteration73 historical result FAILS:July mean767.0085→765.8563(mean per-asset-0.1567%,5/5 wins),August1681.5828→1682.7293(+0.0547%,1/5 wins). DISCARD TimesFM from serving under the registered both-historical-means criterion. Finish the already-running additional September study for completeness. The favorable10/10 development cells and19/20 daily gains do not override this failure. Descriptive two-day block95% intervals on daily mean percentage changes were[-0.2411,-0.0670] and[-0.4844,-0.0975]; these do not adjust for model selection and cannot establish temporal transfer. Large unselected weights remain ignored.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('agent/report.md');s=p.read_text();anchor='## Results\\\\n';s=s.replace(anchor,'TimesFM-1.0-200m improves all10 recent one-hour cells beyond the selected bridge model (mean CRPS922.1419/689.3561), but fails the causal historical August check:1681.5828→1682.7293, with only1/5 assets improving. July improves all five assets. Under the predeclared historical criterion, we reject this learned addition despite its consistent recent gains. Its CPU inference meets latency limits; temporal transfer, rather than serving cost, is the limiting evidence.\\\\n\\\\n'+anchor);s=s.replace('its official CRPS comparison remains pending.','its recent CRPS gains failed the historical criterion.');p.write_text(s)\nPY\n git add agent/journal.md agent/report.md agent/results/historical_timesfm_v9 agent/results/historical_timesfm_v9_suite.log agent/results/timesfm_v9_full_block_intervals.json\n git commit -m 'Reject TimesFM promotion after historical regime reversal'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
