{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_95","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\nIteration75 completed36-cell result:COM also worsens October(+0.0025%,4/8wins),confirming rejection for that group. Crypto24h is the sole retained PCA candidate pending iteration77. Iteration76 additionalSeptember Bolt mean922.5773→921.7095(mean per-asset-0.0995%,4/5wins);historicalAugust rejection remains unchanged.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('agent/report.md');s=p.read_text();anchor='## Results\\\\n';s=s.replace(anchor,'Chronos-Bolt-tiny is faster (approximately0.04s warm CPU path generation) and improves all10 recent one-hour cells, with means922.0844/689.2155. Like TimesFM, it improves July but regresses August (1681.5828→1682.5864), so it also fails the registered transfer criterion. Both direct log-point forecasters improve4/5 cells on addedSeptember. Their repeated temporal reversal is more informative than choosing whichever architecture wins the recent comparison.\\\\n\\\\nPrincipal-component Sobol integration preserves Gaussian covariance algebraically and improves all10 recent crypto24h cells (4199.1576/3404.2744 versus4201.6155/3406.1522). It worsens both means for COM and one-hour crypto. Only the24h crypto sampler remains under independent-seed and temporal validation; serving is unchanged.\\\\n\\\\n'+anchor);p.write_text(s)\nPY\n git add agent/journal.md agent/report.md agent/queue_pca_validation.json agent/results/pca_v9_full agent/results/pca_v9_full_suite.log agent/results/historical_bolt_v9 agent/results/historical_bolt_v9_suite.log agent/results/sep_late_bolt_v9 agent/results/sep_late_bolt_v9_suite.log agent/results/sep_late_chronos_adaptive_v8 agent/results/sep_late_chronos_adaptive_v8_suite.log\n git commit -m 'Document learned-model transfer failures and isolate PCA candidate'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
