{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_249","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc 'cat agent/suggestions.md; cat agent/verify_serving.py; git status --short'","aggregated_output":"# Suggestions for the benchmark and future work\n\n- The campaign says BUDGET.md is at the workspace root; this run's harness writes agent/BUDGET.md. Align the documented location.\n- Keep the raw-context issuance cutoff explicit. The supplied evaluator originally took the last 10080 rows before issuance; the official generator uses the seven calendar days ending at issuance. This run aligns with the official generator.\n- Daily NumPy predictions substantially reduce serialization overhead compared with one JSON file per prompt. The official loader already supports them; make this the default in the starter evaluator.\n- Calendar data sometimes co-locates GDP and PCE. Treat their effects jointly instead of estimating independent additive effects from the same release observations.\n- DATA.md omits the measured scored-prompt span described in CAMPAIGN.md. This bundle starts on September 8, 2026 at approximately 23:00 UTC, despite cached realized paths starting in June. Explicitly report both spans.\n- Official backtest raises KeyError('miner_uid') when a one-prompt window leaves no smoothed-score rows. It should return CRPS with an unavailable rank, or raise a coverage error before prediction generation.\n\n- Expose a supported CRPS-only mode using cached validator prompt schedules when field scores are unavailable. This campaign verified exact parity through the internal official scoring worker, but a public API would remove reliance on private internals.\n- Preserve the official scorer's component totals in backtest output. The validator already computes price-interval and volatility details, but the backtester worker discards them. Keeping them would make distribution-model failures easier to diagnose without changing the metric.\n\"\"\"Serving/reference parity and contract checks on actual sparse snapshot contexts.\"\"\"\nimport argparse,importlib,json,os,time\nimport numpy as np,pandas as pd\nfrom synth_lib.preparation.config import default_store_root\nfrom predict import load_minute_prices,context_end\nimport modeling\np=argparse.ArgumentParser();p.add_argument('--reference',required=True);a=p.parse_args();reference=importlib.import_module(a.reference)\ncrypto=['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE'];assets=crypto+['XAU','NVDAX','GOOGLX','TSLAX','AAPLX','WTIOIL','SPCX','SP500']\nos.environ['MODEL_CONFIG']='{\"scale\":9}'\ncount=0;contexts={}\nfor date in ['2026-09-16','2026-10-08']:\n t=pd.Timestamp(date,tz='UTC')\n for asset in assets:\n  f=load_minute_prices(default_store_root(asset).parents[2],asset,t-pd.Timedelta(days=8),t)\n  for length,step in ([(86400,300),(3600,60)] if asset in crypto else [(86400,300)]):\n   end=context_end(t,length);frame=f.loc[(f.index>end-pd.Timedelta(days=7))&(f.index<=end)]\n   x=modeling.simulate(asset,t,step,length,17,frame);y=reference.simulate(asset,t,step,length,17,frame)\n   assert x==y,(asset,date,length)\n   paths=np.asarray(x[2:]);assert paths.shape==(17,length//step+1)\n   assert np.isfinite(paths).all() and (paths>0).all()\n   assert np.all(paths[:,0]==frame.close.dropna().iloc[-1]);count+=1\n   contexts[(asset,length)]=(t,step,frame)\nlatencies={}\nfor asset,length in [('BTC',3600),('AAPLX',86400),('XAU',86400)]:\n t,step,frame=contexts[(asset,length)];start=time.perf_counter()\n x=modeling.simulate(asset,t,step,length,1000,frame);elapsed=time.perf_counter()-start\n assert len(x)==1002 and np.asarray(x[2:]).shape==(1000,length//step+1)\n y=modeling.simulate(asset,t,step,length,1000,frame);assert x==y\n latencies[asset+'_'+str(length)]={'seconds':elapsed,'context_nan_closes':int(frame.close.isna().sum())}\nt,step,frame=contexts[('BTC',3600)]\nos.environ['SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED']='11';x=modeling.simulate('BTC',t,step,3600,17,frame)\nos.environ['SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED']='37';y=modeling.simulate('BTC',t,step,3600,17,frame)\nassert x!=y\nprint(json.dumps({'reference':a.reference,'exact_parity_calls':count,'arbitrary_count':17,'contract_count':1000,'repeatability':True,'seed_changes_paths':True,'latencies':latencies},indent=2))\n M agent/analyze_events.py\n M agent/evaluate_crps_gradient.py\n M agent/fit_crps_gradient.py\n M agent/journal.md\n M agent/results/forecast_cache_parity.log\n M agent/run_crps_gradient_holdout.py\n?? agent/BUDGET.md\n?? agent/crps_gradient_historical.json\n?? agent/event_multipliers_eventclean.json\n?? agent/event_multipliers_finefloor_control.json\n?? agent/matched_proxy_diagnostic.json\n?? agent/matched_proxy_refit.json\n?? agent/queue_event_joint.json\n?? agent/queue_matched_proxy.json\n?? agent/results/crps_gradient_historical_fit.log\n?? agent/results/crps_gradient_historical_fit_report.json\n?? agent/results/crps_gradient_historical_training_data.parquet\n?? agent/results/crps_slope_historical_BTC.log\n?? agent/results/crps_slope_historical_ETH.log\n?? agent/results/crps_slope_historical_HYPE.log\n?? agent/results/crps_slope_historical_SOL.log\n?? agent/results/crps_slope_historical_XRP.log\n?? agent/results/crps_slope_historical_labels/\n?? agent/results/crps_slopes_historical_suite.log\n?? agent/results/event_diagnostics_eventclean.csv\n?? agent/results/event_diagnostics_eventclean.log\n?? agent/results/event_diagnostics_finefloor_control.csv\n?? agent/results/event_diagnostics_finefloor_control.log\n?? agent/results/event_fit_eventclean.csv\n?? agent/results/event_fit_eventclean.log\n?? agent/results/event_fit_finefloor_control.csv\n?? agent/results/event_fit_finefloor_control.log\n?? agent/results/eventclean_com_v9_full/\n?? agent/results/eventclean_com_v9_full_suite.log\n?? agent/results/eventclean_refit_com/\n?? agent/results/eventclean_refit_com_suite.log\n?? agent/results/gradient_seed11_control/\n?? agent/results/gradient_seed11_control_suite.log\n?? agent/results/gradient_seed11_tree/\n?? agent/results/gradient_seed11_tr